  wait: {
    usage: ["dagyard wait <node> [--blocker <id>] [--timeout <sec>] [--json]", "dagyard wait <nodo> [--blocker <id>] [--timeout <seg>] [--json]"],
    summary: ["waits for the person to answer and prints the answer", "espera a que el humano resuelva y devuelve la resoluci\xF3n"],
    help: [
      `Without --blocker it waits on the node's latest open blocker (or prints the latest answered one).
First line: the chosen option (or the access value). If there is a note, \xABnote: \u2026\xBB follows.
Without --timeout it waits forever. Exit 2 when it runs out.`,
      `Sin --blocker espera el \xFAltimo bloqueante abierto del nodo (o devuelve el \xFAltimo resuelto).
Primera l\xEDnea: la opci\xF3n elegida (o el valor del acceso). Si hay nota, sigue \xABnota: \u2026\xBB.
Sin --timeout espera para siempre. Exit 2 si vence.`
    ],
    flags: ["blocker", "timeout", ...GLOBAL_FLAGS],
    bools: ["json"],
    async run({ io, args }) {
      const [id] = need(args, [["node", "nodo"]]);
      const timeoutRaw = flag(args, "timeout");
      const timeout = timeoutRaw === void 0 ? 0 : Number(timeoutRaw);
      if (!Number.isFinite(timeout) || timeout < 0) throw new UsageError(t("--timeout is in seconds (\u22650)", "--timeout va en segundos (\u22650)"));
      const sleep = io.sleep ?? ((ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms)));
      const api = client(io, args);
      const proj = project(io, args);
      const blockerId = flag(args, "blocker") ?? await blockerOf(api, proj, nodeId(id));
      const deadline = timeout > 0 ? Date.now() + timeout * 1e3 : Infinity;
      let failures = 0;
      for (; ; ) {
        const left = Math.ceil((deadline - Date.now()) / 1e3);
        if (left <= 0) {
          io.stderr(t(`dagyard: nobody answered the blocker on ${nodeId(id)} within ${timeout} s
`, `dagyard: nadie resolvi\xF3 el bloqueante de ${nodeId(id)} en ${timeout} s
`));
          return EXIT.timeout;
        }
        let result;
        try {
          result = await api.waitOnce(proj, blockerId, Math.min(25, left));
          failures = 0;
        } catch (err) {
          if (err instanceof ApiRequestError && waitTransient(err)) {
            const backoff = WAIT_BACKOFF_MS[Math.min(failures++, WAIT_BACKOFF_MS.length - 1)];
            await sleep(Math.max(0, Math.min(backoff, deadline - Date.now())));
            continue;
          }
          throw err;
        }
        if (result) {
          io.stdout(args.bools.has("json") ? `${JSON.stringify(result)}
` : formatResolution(result));
          return EXIT.ok;
        }
      }
    }
  },
  watch: {
    usage: [
      "dagyard watch [--since <seq>] [--cursor <file>] [--interval <sec>] [--once] [--json]",
      "dagyard watch [--since <seq>] [--cursor <archivo>] [--interval <seg>] [--once] [--json]"
    ],
    summary: ["listens to the project's questions and answers, one line each", "escucha las preguntas y respuestas del proyecto, una l\xEDnea por cada una"],
    help: [
      `For whoever orchestrates: one line per blocker opened (\xABasks\xBB) or answered (\xABanswered\xBB, with the option and the
note), each with its event number (#seq). Runs until killed.
Without --since it starts now and first lists the blockers already open (\xABstill waiting\xBB); --since <seq> replays
what came after that event. --cursor <file> keeps the last event seen there and, without --since, resumes from it.
If the server no longer has the events after --since (\xABresync\xBB), it says so and goes on from the current state.
Checks every --interval seconds (default 5). --once catches up and exits 0.
If the server stops answering it retries with backoff; after ~1.5 min it exits 4 saying how to resume.`,
      `Para quien orquesta: una l\xEDnea por bloqueante abierto (\xABpregunta\xBB) o respondido (\xABrespondieron\xBB, con la opci\xF3n y
la nota), cada una con su n\xFAmero de evento (#seq). Corre hasta que lo maten.
Sin --since empieza ahora y antes lista los bloqueantes ya abiertos (\xABsigue esperando\xBB); --since <seq> repite lo
que vino despu\xE9s de ese evento. --cursor <archivo> guarda ah\xED el \xFAltimo evento visto y, sin --since, reanuda desde \xE9l.
Si el servidor ya no tiene los eventos despu\xE9s de --since (\xABresync\xBB), lo avisa y sigue desde el estado actual.
Mira cada --interval segundos (5 por defecto). --once se pone al d\xEDa y sale 0.
Si el servidor deja de responder reintenta con backoff; tras ~1,5 min sale 4 y dice c\xF3mo reanudar.`
    ],
    flags: ["since", "cursor", "interval", ...GLOBAL_FLAGS],
    bools: ["once", "json"],
    async run({ io, args }) {
      const sinceRaw = flag(args, "since");
      const cursor = flag(args, "cursor");
      let since = sinceRaw === void 0 ? null : seqArg(sinceRaw, "--since");
      if (since === null && cursor !== void 0) since = readCursor(cursor);
      const intervalRaw = flag(args, "interval");
      const interval = intervalRaw === void 0 ? 5 : Number(intervalRaw);
      if (!Number.isFinite(interval) || interval < 1) throw new UsageError(t("--interval is in seconds (\u22651)", "--interval va en segundos (\u22651)"));
      const result = await watch({
        api: client(io, args),
        project: project(io, args),
        since,
        intervalMs: interval * 1e3,
        once: args.bools.has("once"),
        json: args.bools.has("json"),
        out: io.stdout,
        err: io.stderr,
        sleep: io.sleep ?? ((ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms))),
        ...cursor !== void 0 ? { saveCursor: (seq) => writeCursor(cursor, seq) } : {}
      });
      return result === "ok" ? EXIT.ok : EXIT.unreachable;
    }
  },
  msg: {
    usage: ['dagyard msg <node> "\u2026" [--report <url>] [--from "\u2026"]', 'dagyard msg <nodo> "\u2026" [--report <url>] [--from "\u2026"]'],
    summary: [`writes a short note to the PM (\u2264${LIMITS.message} characters)`, `le escribe al PM en corto (\u2264${LIMITS.message} caracteres)`],
    help: ["By default the server fills in --from (the team name).", "--from por defecto lo pone el servidor (\xABEquipo de <equipo>\xBB)."],
    flags: ["report", "from", ...GLOBAL_FLAGS],
    async run({ io, args }) {
      const [id] = need(args, [["node", "nodo"], ["text", "texto"]]);
      const text = args.positionals.slice(1).join(" ").trim();
      if (!text) throw new UsageError(t("the message is empty", "el mensaje est\xE1 vac\xEDo"));
      if ([...text].length > LIMITS.message) {
        const len = [...text].length;
        throw new UsageError(t(`the message has ${len} characters; the limit is ${LIMITS.message}`, `el mensaje tiene ${len} caracteres; el m\xE1ximo es ${LIMITS.message}`));
      }
      const input = { text };
      const from = optional(args, "from", LIMITS.name);
      if (from !== void 0) input.from = from;
      const report = optional(args, "report", LIMITS.url);
      if (report !== void 0) input.reportUrl = report;
      const message = await client(io, args).postMessage(project(io, args), nodeId(id), input);
      io.stdout(`${message?.id ?? "ok"}
`);
      return EXIT.ok;
    }
  },
  next: {
    usage: ["dagyard next [--project <p>] [--json]", "dagyard next [--project <p>] [--json]"],
    summary: ["the next task ready to start, with its /goal line ready to paste", "la siguiente tarea arrancable, con su l\xEDnea /goal lista para pegar"],
    help: [
      `Prints a single line: /goal <mission>; the task's link in the sky goes separately, on stderr
(\xABin the sky: \u2026\xBB), so the output pastes as is. --json carries it in \xABlink\xBB. Exit 3 when nothing is ready to start.`,
      `Imprime una sola l\xEDnea: /goal <misi\xF3n>; el link de la tarea en el cielo va aparte, por stderr
(\xABen el cielo: \u2026\xBB), as\xED la salida se pega tal cual. --json lo trae en \xABlink\xBB. Exit 3 si no hay nada arrancable.`
    ],
    flags: [...GLOBAL_FLAGS],
    bools: ["json"],
    async run({ io, args }) {
      need(args, []);
      const proj = project(io, args);
      const srv = server(io, args);
      const res = await client(io, args, srv).next(proj);
      const link = res.node ? skyLink(srv.url, proj, res.node.id) : null;
      if (args.bools.has("json")) {
        io.stdout(`${JSON.stringify({ ...res, link })}
`);
        return res.goalLine ? EXIT.ok : EXIT.nothing;
      }
      if (!res.goalLine) {
        io.stderr(t(`dagyard: no task is ready to start in ${proj}
`, `dagyard: no hay tareas arrancables en ${proj}
`));
        return EXIT.nothing;
      }
      io.stdout(`${goalLine(res.goalLine)}
`);
      if (link) io.stderr(t(`in the sky: ${link}
`, `en el cielo: ${link}
`));
      return EXIT.ok;
    }
  },
  open: {
