  "import-ledger": {
    usage: [
      "dagyard import-ledger [<sites.jsonl>] [--repo <repo>] [--dry-run] [--json]",
      "dagyard import-ledger [<sites.jsonl>] [--repo <repo>] [--dry-run] [--json]"
    ],
    summary: ["brings the factory's history in as teams, with its dates", "trae la historia de la f\xE1brica como equipos, con sus fechas"],
    help: [
      `By default it reads ~/cofoundy/.coordination/factory/sites.jsonl (JSONL, or a JSON array) and keeps the rows of
--repo (by default the repo of the current folder, from its origin remote). Each site becomes a team: requested,
started and closed with the site's own dates, its issues as gh-<n> tasks. The ledger wins on the dates it knows and
never erases what it does not know. Idempotent: running it again sends nothing. --dry-run reads but writes nothing.`,
      `Por defecto lee ~/cofoundy/.coordination/factory/sites.jsonl (JSONL, o un array JSON) y se queda con las filas de
--repo (por defecto el repo de la carpeta actual, por su remoto origin). Cada sitio es un equipo: pedido, arrancado
y cerrado con las fechas del sitio, sus issues como tareas gh-<n>. El ledger manda en las fechas que conoce y nunca
borra lo que no conoce. Idempotente: correrlo otra vez no manda nada. --dry-run lee pero no escribe nada.`
    ],
    flags: ["repo", ...GLOBAL_FLAGS],
    bools: ["dry-run", "json"],
    async run({ io, args }) {
      if (args.positionals.length > 1) throw new UsageError(extra(args.positionals[1]));
      const file = args.positionals[0] ?? join3(io.env.HOME || homedir2(), "cofoundy", ".coordination", "factory", "sites.jsonl");
      let parsed;
      try {
        parsed = parseLedger(readFileSync3(file, "utf8"));
      } catch (err) {
        const why = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);
        throw new UsageError(t(`could not read the ledger ${file}: ${why}`, `no pude leer el ledger ${file}: ${why}`));
      }
      const needsRepo = parsed.rows.some((r) => typeof r.repo === "string");
      const repo = optional(args, "repo") || (needsRepo ? repoOf(io.cwd ?? process.cwd()) : null);
      if (needsRepo && !repo) {
        throw new UsageError(t("missing --repo: I could not tell the repo of the current folder", "falta --repo: no pude saber el repo de la carpeta actual"));
      }
      const { teams, skipped } = teamsFromLedger(parsed.rows, repo);
      const proj = project(io, args);
      const api = client(io, args);
      const snap = await api.snapshot(proj);
      const current2 = new Map((snap.teams ?? []).map((tm) => [tm.id, tm]));
      const plan = teams.map((l) => {
        const patch = teamPatchFromLedger(l, current2.get(l.id));
        const isNew = !current2.has(l.id);
        const name = isNew ? nameFromTasks(l, snap.nodes) : void 0;
        if (patch && name) patch.name = name;
        const action = isNew ? "created" : patch ? "updated" : "unchanged";
        return { id: l.id, action, patch };
      });
      const dry = args.bools.has("dry-run");
      if (!dry)
        for (const p2 of plan) {
          if (!p2.patch) continue;
          try {
            await api.putTeam(proj, p2.id, p2.patch);
          } catch (err) {
            if (!(err instanceof ApiRequestError)) throw err;
            p2.action = "failed";
            p2.error = `${err.code}: ${err.message}`;
          }
        }
      const report = { file, repo, project: proj, dryRun: dry, skipped, invalid: parsed.invalid, teams: plan };
      io.stdout(args.bools.has("json") ? `${JSON.stringify(report, null, 2)}
` : formatLedger(report));
      const failed = plan.filter((p2) => p2.action === "failed");
      for (const p2 of failed) io.stderr(`dagyard: ${p2.id}: ${p2.error}
`);
      return failed.length ? EXIT.api : EXIT.ok;
    }
  },
  sync: {
    usage: [
      "dagyard sync --github <owner/repo> [--label <l>] [--stage <stage>] [--all] [--dry-run] [--json]",
      "dagyard sync --github <owner/repo> [--label <l>] [--stage <etapa>] [--all] [--dry-run] [--json]"
    ],
    summary: ["creates or updates the gh-<n> tasks from GitHub issues", "crea o actualiza las tareas gh-<n> desde los issues de GitHub"],
    help: [
      `Uses gh (GitHub CLI), signed in. It never replaces the graph: it only adds and moves forward, every change live.
New task = open issue (with --all also the closed ones, already Done), in --stage, or the build stage (Build /
Construcci\xF3n), or the first stage, with the link to the issue. --stage takes the id or the name, in either language,
and sync never creates a stage. A decision with no options in the body offers Yes / No in the project's language.
On an existing task it never changes title, stage, team or mission; the link, only if it
has none. Status only moves forward: closed \u2192 Done; open with an open PR that says \xABcloses #n\xBB \u2192 In progress.
\xABPart of #n\xBB \u2192 task n needs this one; \xABdepends on #n\xBB, \xABblocked by #n\xBB or \xABbloqueado por #n\xBB \u2192 this one needs n.
The founder-input label opens a decision with the options from the body (- **A:** \u2026, - A) \u2026), only if the task
has no decision yet (open or answered). The epic label creates no task.
--dry-run reads but writes nothing.`,
      `Usa gh (GitHub CLI) autenticado. Nunca reemplaza el grafo: solo agrega y avanza, cada cambio en vivo.
Tarea nueva = issue abierto (con --all tambi\xE9n los cerrados, ya Listos), en --stage, o la de construcci\xF3n (Build /
Construcci\xF3n), o la primera etapa, con el enlace al issue. --stage acepta el id o el nombre, en cualquiera de los dos
idiomas, y sync nunca crea una etapa. Una decisi\xF3n sin opciones en el cuerpo ofrece S\xED / No en el idioma del proyecto.
A una tarea que ya existe nunca le cambia t\xEDtulo, etapa, equipo ni misi\xF3n; el enlace, solo si
no tiene. El estado solo avanza: cerrado \u2192 Lista; abierto con un PR abierto que dice \xABcloses #n\xBB \u2192 En progreso.
\xABParte de #n\xBB \u2192 la tarea n necesita esta; \xABdepende de #n\xBB, \xABblocked by #n\xBB o \xABbloqueado por #n\xBB \u2192 esta necesita la n.
La etiqueta founder-input abre una decisi\xF3n con las opciones del cuerpo (- **A:** \u2026, - A) \u2026), solo si la tarea
no tiene ya una decisi\xF3n (abierta o respondida). La etiqueta epic no crea tarea.
--dry-run lee pero no escribe nada.`
    ],
    flags: ["github", "label", "stage", ...GLOBAL_FLAGS],
    bools: ["all", "dry-run", "json"],
    async run({ io, args }) {
      need(args, []);
      const repo = required(args, "github");
      if (!/^[\w.-]+\/[\w.-]+$/.test(repo) || repo.split("/").some((seg) => seg === "." || seg.includes(".."))) {
        throw new UsageError(t(`--github goes as owner/repo: \xAB${repo}\xBB`, `--github va como owner/repo: \xAB${repo}\xBB`));
      }
      const label = optional(args, "label");
      const stage = optional(args, "stage");
      const report = await syncGithub(client(io, args), io.github ?? ghCliSource(), project(io, args), {
        repo,
        ...label ? { label } : {},
        ...stage ? { stage } : {},
        all: args.bools.has("all"),
        dryRun: args.bools.has("dry-run")
      });
      io.stdout(args.bools.has("json") ? `${JSON.stringify(report, null, 2)}
` : formatSync(report));
      return EXIT.ok;
    }
  }
};
var SHORTCUTS = { start: "node start", progress: "node progress", done: "node done" };
async function run(argv, io) {
  return withLang(langFromEnv(io.env), () => runIn(argv, io));
}
async function runIn(argv, io) {
  let key = null;
  try {
    key = loadKey(io.env);
    const lead = leadingGlobals(argv);
    argv = lead.rest;
    const [first, second] = argv;
    if (!first || first === "help" || first === "--help" || first === "-h") {
      io.stdout(globalHelp());
      return EXIT.ok;
    }
    if (first === "--version" || first === "-v" || first === "version") {
      io.stdout(`${VERSION}
`);
      return EXIT.ok;
    }
    let name;
    let rest;
    if (first === "node" || first === "edge" || first === "team" || first === "goal" || first === "request") {
      if (!second || second.startsWith("-")) {
        io.stdout(groupHelp(first));
        return second && !["--help", "-h"].includes(second) ? EXIT.usage : EXIT.ok;
      }
      name = `${first} ${second}`;
      rest = argv.slice(2);
    } else {
      name = SHORTCUTS[first] ?? first;
      rest = argv.slice(1);
    }
    const cmd = COMMANDS[name];
    if (!cmd) throw new UsageError(t(`unknown command \xAB${name}\xBB`, `no conozco el comando \xAB${name}\xBB`));
    const args = parseArgs([...lead.globals, ...rest], cmd.bools ?? []);
    if (args.bools.has("help")) {
      io.stdout(commandHelp(cmd));
      return EXIT.ok;
    }
    assertKnownFlags(args, cmd.flags);
    for (const b of args.bools) {
      if (b !== "help" && !(cmd.bools ?? []).includes(b)) throw new UsageError(t(`unknown option: --${b}`, `opci\xF3n desconocida: --${b}`));
    }
    return await cmd.run({ io, args });
  } catch (err) {
    const redact = (s) => key ? s.split(key).join("***") : s;
    if (err instanceof UsageError) {
      const hint = t("See \xABdagyard --help\xBB or \xABdagyard <command> --help\xBB.", "Usa \xABdagyard --help\xBB o \xABdagyard <comando> --help\xBB.");
      io.stderr(redact(`dagyard: ${err.message}
${hint}
`));
      return EXIT.usage;
    }
    if (err instanceof ApiRequestError) {
      io.stderr(redact(`dagyard: ${err.code}: ${err.message}
`));
      return EXIT.api;
    }
    io.stderr(redact(`dagyard: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}
`));
    return EXIT.api;
  }
}
function leadingGlobals(argv) {
  const globals = [];
  let i = 0;
  for (; i < argv.length; i++) {
    const m = /^(?:--(project|url)|-(p))(=.*)?$/.exec(argv[i]);
    if (!m) break;
    globals.push(argv[i]);
    if (m[3] !== void 0) continue;
    const value = argv[i + 1];
    const opt = m[1] ?? "project";
    if (value === void 0) throw new UsageError(t(`--${opt} needs a value`, `a --${opt} le falta el valor`));
    globals.push(value);
    i++;
  }
  return { globals, rest: argv.slice(i) };
}
function config(io, skipRepoUrl) {
  return loadConfig(io.env, io.cwd ?? process.cwd(), { warn: io.stderr, skipRepoUrl });
}
function server(io, args) {
  const urlFlag = flag(args, "url");
  const cfg = config(io, urlFlag !== void 0);
  const url2 = urlFlag ?? cfg.url;
  if (!url2) {
    throw new UsageError(
      t("missing server: --url, DAGYARD_URL, .dagyard.json or ~/.config/dagyard/url", "falta el servidor: --url, DAGYARD_URL, .dagyard.json o ~/.config/dagyard/url")
    );
  }
  return { url: url2, key: cfg.key };
}
function client(io, args, srv = server(io, args)) {
  if (!srv.key) throw new UsageError(t("missing API key: DAGYARD_KEY or ~/.config/dagyard/agent-key", "falta la API key: DAGYARD_KEY o ~/.config/dagyard/agent-key"));
  return new DagyardClient({ baseUrl: srv.url, key: srv.key, ...io.fetch ? { fetch: io.fetch } : {}, ...io.sleep ? { sleep: io.sleep } : {} });
}
function openInBrowser(link) {
  return new Promise((resolve3, reject) => {
    const child = spawn("open", [link], { stdio: "ignore" });
    child.on("error", reject);
    child.on("exit", (code2) => code2 === 0 ? resolve3() : reject(new Error(t(`open exited with ${code2}`, `open sali\xF3 con ${code2}`))));
  });
}
function project(io, args) {
  const p2 = flag(args, "project") ?? config(io, true).project;
  if (!p2) {
    throw new UsageError(
      t(
        "missing project: --project, DAGYARD_PROJECT, .dagyard.json or ~/.config/dagyard/project",
        "falta el proyecto: --project, DAGYARD_PROJECT, .dagyard.json o ~/.config/dagyard/project"
      )
    );
  }
  return slugify(p2);
}
function need(args, names) {
  const missing = names.slice(args.positionals.length);
  if (missing.length) {
    const name = tx(missing[0]);
    throw new UsageError(t(`missing <${name}>`, `falta <${name}>`));
  }
  if (names.length === 0 && args.positionals.length) throw new UsageError(extra(args.positionals[0]));
  return args.positionals;
}
function siteId(raw) {
  const v = raw.trim();
  if (isSlug(v)) return v;
  if (!/[a-z0-9]/i.test(raw.normalize("NFD"))) throw new UsageError(t(`\xAB${raw}\xBB is not a usable site id`, `\xAB${raw}\xBB no sirve como id de sitio`));
  return slugify(raw.trim());
}
function atArg(args) {
  const raw = optional(args, "at");
  if (raw === void 0) return void 0;
  const at = normalizeIso(raw);
  if (!at) throw new UsageError(t(`--at is an ISO 8601 date with time and zone (2026-10-04T05:35:20Z): \xAB${raw}\xBB`, `--at va como fecha ISO 8601 con hora y zona (2026-10-04T05:35:20Z): \xAB${raw}\xBB`));
  return at;
}
function issuesArg(args) {
  const out = [];
  for (const part of (args.flags.issues ?? []).flatMap((v) => v.split(","))) {
    const n = part.trim().replace(/^(?:gh-|#)/i, "");
    if (!n) continue;
    if (!/^\d+$/.test(n)) throw new UsageError(t(`--issues takes issue numbers: \xAB${part.trim()}\xBB`, `--issues lleva n\xFAmeros de issue: \xAB${part.trim()}\xBB`));
    if (!out.includes(`gh-${n}`)) out.push(`gh-${n}`);
  }
  return out;
}
async function currentTeam(api, proj, tid) {
  return (await api.snapshot(proj)).teams?.find((tm) => tm.id === tid);
}
function repoOf(cwd) {
  const git = (...a) => execFileSync("git", ["-C", cwd, ...a], { encoding: "utf8", stdio: ["ignore", "pipe", "ignore"] }).trim();
  try {
    const m = /([^/:]+?)(?:\.git)?\/?$/.exec(git("remote", "get-url", "origin"));
    if (m) return m[1];
  } catch {
  }
  try {
    return basename2(git("rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")) || null;
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
function nameFromTasks(l, nodes) {
  for (const id of l.nodeIds) {
    const team = nodes.find((n) => n.id === id)?.team?.trim();
    if (team && !/^(f[áa]brica|factory)$/i.test(team)) return team;
  }
  return void 0;
}
function formatLedger(r) {
  const count = (a) => r.teams.filter((x) => x.action === a).length;
  const head = r.dryRun ? t("(dry run, nothing sent) ", "(simulaci\xF3n, no envi\xE9 nada) ") : "";
  const of = r.repo ? t(` of ${r.repo}`, ` de ${r.repo}`) : "";
  const lines = [
    head + t(
      `${plural(r.teams.length, ["team", "teams"], ["equipo", "equipos"])} in the ledger${of} \u2192 ${r.project}: ${count("created")} new, ${count("updated")} updated, ${count("unchanged")} unchanged`,
      `${plural(r.teams.length, ["team", "teams"], ["equipo", "equipos"])} en el ledger${of} \u2192 ${r.project}: ${count("created")} nuevos, ${count("updated")} actualizados, ${count("unchanged")} sin cambios`
    )
  ];
  for (const x of r.teams) {
    if (x.action === "created") lines.push(`  + ${x.id}${x.patch?.name ? ` \xAB${x.patch.name}\xBB` : ""}`);
    else if (x.action === "updated") lines.push(`  ~ ${x.id} (${Object.keys(x.patch ?? {}).join(", ")})`);
  }
  for (const x of r.teams) if (x.action === "failed") lines.push(`  ! ${x.id}`);
  if (count("failed")) lines.push(t(`  ${count("failed")} rejected by the server (see stderr)`, `  ${count("failed")} rechazados por el servidor (mira stderr)`));
  if (r.invalid) lines.push(t(`  ${r.invalid} unreadable rows skipped`, `  ${r.invalid} filas ilegibles ignoradas`));
  return `${lines.join("\n")}
`;
}
function extra(arg) {
  return t(`unexpected \xAB${arg}\xBB`, `sobra \xAB${arg}\xBB`);
}
function nodeId(raw) {
  if (!/[a-z0-9]/i.test(raw.normalize("NFD"))) throw new UsageError(t(`\xAB${raw}\xBB is not a usable node id`, `\xAB${raw}\xBB no sirve como id de nodo`));
  return slugify(raw);
}
var WAIT_BACKOFF_MS = [1e3, 2e3, 5e3, 1e4];
var waitTransient = (err) => err.status === 0 || err.status >= 500 || err.status === 429;
async function blockerOf(api, proj, node) {
  const mine = (await api.snapshot(proj)).blockers.filter((b) => b.nodeId === node).sort((a, b) => a.createdAt.localeCompare(b.createdAt));
  const pick = mine.filter((b) => b.status === "open").pop() ?? mine.pop();
  if (!pick) throw new UsageError(t(`${node} has no blockers; open one with \xABdagyard block ${node} \u2026\xBB`, `${node} no tiene bloqueantes; \xE1brelo con \xABdagyard block ${node} \u2026\xBB`));
  return pick.id;
}
function seqArg(raw, name) {
  if (!/^\d+$/.test(raw.trim())) throw new UsageError(t(`${name} is an event number (an integer \u22650)`, `${name} es un n\xFAmero de evento (un entero \u22650)`));
  return Number(raw.trim());
}
function readCursor(file) {
  let raw;
  try {
    raw = readFileSync3(file, "utf8");
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.code === "ENOENT") return null;
    throw err;
  }
  return seqArg(raw, file);
}
function writeCursor(file, seq) {
  mkdirSync(dirname3(file), { recursive: true });
  const tmp = `${file}.${process.pid}.tmp`;
  writeFileSync(tmp, `${seq}
`);
  renameSync(tmp, file);
}
function required(args, key, max) {
  const v = optional(args, key, max);
  if (v === void 0 || v === "") throw new UsageError(t(`missing --${key}`, `falta --${key}`));
  return v;
}
function optional(args, key, max) {
  const v = flag(args, key)?.trim();
  if (v !== void 0 && max !== void 0 && [...v].length > max) {
    throw new UsageError(t(`--${key} is at most ${max} characters`, `--${key} va hasta ${max} caracteres`));
  }
  return v;
}
function linkArg(args) {
  const link = optional(args, "link", LIMITS.url);
  if (link !== void 0 && !/^https?:\/\/\S+$/i.test(link)) {
    throw new UsageError(t(`--link must be an http(s) URL (the issue or PR one): \xAB${link}\xBB`, `--link debe ser una URL http(s) (la del issue o del PR): \xAB${link}\xBB`));
  }
  return link;
}
function kindArg(args) {
  const k = flag(args, "kind");
  if (k === void 0) return void 0;
  const kinds = NODE_KINDS.join(", ");
  if (!NODE_KINDS.includes(k)) throw new UsageError(t(`--kind must be ${kinds}`, `--kind debe ser ${kinds}`));
  return k;
}
function originsArg(args) {
  const out = [];
  for (const [k, v] of args.seq) {
    if (k === "from") {
      out.push({ from: nodeId(v) });
      continue;
    }
    if (k !== "why") continue;
    const last = out[out.length - 1];
    if (!last || last.why !== void 0) throw new UsageError(t("each --why goes right after its --from", "cada --why va justo despu\xE9s de su --from"));
    const why = v.trim();
    if ([...why].length > LIMITS.originWhy) throw new UsageError(t(`--why is at most ${LIMITS.originWhy} characters`, `--why va hasta ${LIMITS.originWhy} caracteres`));
    if (why) last.why = why;
  }
  return out;
}
function statusArg(s) {
  if (s === "blocked") throw new UsageError(t("blocked is not set by hand: \xABdagyard block\xBB sets it", "blocked no se pone a mano: lo pone \xABdagyard block\xBB"));
  if (!NODE_STATUSES.includes(s)) throw new UsageError(t(`--status must be ${MANUAL_STATUSES}`, `--status debe ser ${MANUAL_STATUSES}`));
  return s;
}
var MANUAL_STATUSES = NODE_STATUSES.filter((s) => s !== "blocked").join(", ");
function progressArg(raw) {
  const pct = raw.trim().endsWith("%");
  let n = Number(raw.trim().replace(/%$/, ""));
  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) throw new UsageError(t(`invalid progress: \xAB${raw}\xBB`, `avance inv\xE1lido: \xAB${raw}\xBB`));
  if (pct || n > 1) n /= 100;
  if (n < 0 || n > 1) throw new UsageError(t(`progress goes from 0 to 1 (or 0% to 100%): \xAB${raw}\xBB`, `el avance va de 0 a 1 (o de 0% a 100%): \xAB${raw}\xBB`));
  return Math.round(n * 1e3) / 1e3;
}
function skyLink(base, projectId, node) {
  const p2 = `?p=${encodeURIComponent(projectId)}`;
  return `${base.replace(/\/+$/, "")}/${p2}${node ? `&n=${encodeURIComponent(node)}` : ""}`;
}
function goalLine(raw) {
  const line = oneLine(raw, 1e4);
  return line.startsWith("/goal ") ? line : `/goal ${line.replace(/^\/goal\b\s*/, "")}`;
}
function formatResolution(r) {
  const res = r.blocker.resolution;
  const first = r.blocker.kind === "access" ? r.value ?? "" : res?.choice ?? "";
  return `${first}
${res?.note ? `${t("note", "nota")}: ${oneLine(res.note, 1e4)}
` : ""}`;
}
async function existingProjectLang(api, pid) {
  try {
    return projectLang((await api.snapshot(pid)).project);
  } catch (err) {
    if (err instanceof ApiRequestError && err.status === 404) return null;
    throw err;
  }
}
function formatImport(r, dry, replace) {
  const s = r.stats;
  const how = s.stageSource === "phase" ? t("by phase", "por fase") : t("by depth", "por profundidad");
  const done = replace ? t(" \u2014 replaced", " \u2014 reemplazado") : t(" \u2014 imported", " \u2014 importado");
  const st = s.status;
  const lines = [
    t(
      `Project \xAB${r.graph.name}\xBB (${r.projectId})${dry ? " \u2014 dry run, nothing was sent" : done}`,
      `Proyecto \xAB${r.graph.name}\xBB (${r.projectId})${dry ? " \u2014 simulaci\xF3n, no se envi\xF3 nada" : done}`
    ),
    [
      plural(s.nodes, ["task", "tasks"], ["nodo", "nodos"]),
      plural(s.edges, ["dependency", "dependencies"], ["arista", "aristas"]),
      `${plural(s.stages.length, ["stage", "stages"], ["etapa", "etapas"])} (${how})`
    ].join(" \xB7 "),
    ...s.stages.map((stage) => `  ${stage.name}: ${stage.nodes}`),
    // desde #35 el import nunca manda `blocked`: «te esperan» siempre daba 0 (#38); se cuentan los avisos
    [
      t(
        `Status: ${st.pending} pending \xB7 ${st.working} in progress \xB7 ${st.done} done`,
        `Estados: ${st.pending} pendientes \xB7 ${st.working} en progreso \xB7 ${st.done} listas`
      ),
      ...s.asksHuman ? [
        s.asksHuman === 1 ? t("1 asks a person for something", "1 pide algo a una persona") : t(`${s.asksHuman} ask a person for something`, `${s.asksHuman} piden algo a una persona`)
      ] : []
    ].join(" \xB7 ")
  ];
  if (s.titled !== void 0) lines.push(t(`Titles from --titles: ${s.titled} of ${s.nodes}`, `T\xEDtulos de --titles: ${s.titled} de ${s.nodes}`));
  if (r.warnings.length) {
    lines.push(t(`Warnings (${r.warnings.length}):`, `Avisos (${r.warnings.length}):`), ...r.warnings.map((w) => `  - ${w}`));
  }
  return `${lines.join("\n")}
`;
}
function globalHelp() {
  const rows = Object.entries(COMMANDS).map(([name, c]) => `  ${name.padEnd(14)} ${tx(c.summary)}`);
  return t(
    `dagyard ${VERSION} \u2014 the factory's plan as a live DAG

Usage: dagyard <command> [options]

Commands:
${rows.join("\n")}
  start | progress | done   shortcuts for node start | node progress | node done

${tx(HELP_GLOBAL)}
`,
    `dagyard ${VERSION} \u2014 el plan de la f\xE1brica como un DAG vivo

Uso: dagyard <comando> [opciones]

Comandos:
${rows.join("\n")}
  start | progress | done   atajos de node start | node progress | node done

${tx(HELP_GLOBAL)}
`
  );
}
function groupHelp(group) {
  const rows = Object.entries(COMMANDS).filter(([name]) => name.startsWith(`${group} `)).map(([, c]) => `  ${tx(c.usage)}
      ${tx(c.summary)}`);
  return `${t("Usage", "Uso")}:
${rows.join("\n")}

${tx(HELP_GLOBAL)}
`;
}
function commandHelp(c) {
  const summary = tx(c.summary);
  return `${t("Usage", "Uso")}: ${tx(c.usage)}

${summary.charAt(0).toUpperCase()}${summary.slice(1)}.
${tx(c.help)}

${tx(HELP_GLOBAL)}
`;
}

// src/main.ts
var code = await run(process.argv.slice(2), {
  stdout: (s) => process.stdout.write(s),
  stderr: (s) => process.stderr.write(s),
  env: process.env
});
process.exitCode = code;
